  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "The top Divider steps the chords on every downbeat, and its **Gate** holds the Vocoder's **Freeze** for three beats. On beat 4 it lets go: the next vowel flows into the bands, and the downbeat freezes it onto the new chord.",
      "position": [
        40.0,
        770.0
      ],
      "width": 396.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The lower Divider starts the singer on beat 4. It sings one vowel a bar, on the last beat, on a note the chord it leaves and the chord it's sung for share. Every other beat is a held vowel.",
      "position": [
        524.0,
        700.0
      ],
      "width": 230.0
    },
    {
      "text": "**Flatten** at 100% lets a soft triangle pad speak its vowels. Turn it down to 0 and the \"ee\" goes dull. Unmute **3** on the Mixer to hear the singer itself.",
      "position": [
        840.0,
        530.0
      ],
      "width": 230.0
    }
  ]
